@page "/lessons"

<PageTitle>Lessons | CodeLogic</PageTitle>

<HeadContent>
    <meta name="description" content="Preview the planned CodeLogic path for learning C# fundamentals." />
</HeadContent>

<section class="page-header" aria-labelledby="lessons-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">Lessons</p>
    <h1 id="lessons-title">Build your C# foundation</h1>
    <p>Lesson content is not available yet. This preview shows the planned direction without pretending the curriculum has been implemented.</p>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="lesson-preview-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
        <h2 id="lesson-preview-title">Planned starting topics</h2>
        <p>The curriculum specification and first complete lessons belong to Prompt 07.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card-grid">
        <article class="feature-card">
            <p class="status-badge">Planned</p>
            <h3>Variables and types</h3>
            <p>Learn how names, types, and values work together in a simple C# program.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="feature-card">
            <p class="status-badge">Planned</p>
            <h3>Decisions</h3>
            <p>Follow an <code>if</code>/<code>else</code> condition and understand why one path is selected.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="feature-card">
            <p class="status-badge">Planned</p>
            <h3>Loops</h3>
            <p>Trace repeated work and identify a loop's starting point, condition, body, and update.</p>
        </article>
    </div>
</section>

<aside class="notice" aria-labelledby="lesson-notice-title">
    <h2 id="lesson-notice-title">What works today?</h2>
    <p>Navigation and the responsive application shell are ready. Lessons, exercises, and completion state are deliberately deferred.</p>
</aside>
